  "findings": [
    "A=s.castSucc and B=s.succ are consecutive physical positions in the linear child boundary word. The old embedding skips exactly B, retaining s at A. Its numeric formula shifts exactly positions strictly after s. These definitions concern occurrences, not the existing cyclic edge labels.",
    "collapse=s.predAbove is monotone, sends both A and B to s and is a left inverse of the strict old embedding. Every child position except B is recovered as old(collapse p), so child exhaustion and each stated fiber are actual map equalities.",
    "The fiber over s is exactly {A,B}; every other core position has exactly the one old preimage. The zero and last distinguished positions are included. There is no n>=3 or interior-s premise in these helpers; the source domain is contained in their domain.",
    "For p<q the numeric collapse formula proves equality precisely when p=A and q=B. Monotonicity then gives strictness for every other increasing pair. Thus the only child BoundaryInterval with coincident collapsed endpoints is duplicateInterval=[A,B], whose leaf count is1. Every other collapseInterval derives its increasing field from the proved exception characterization.",
    "Root first59431 failed only on an implicit Fin lemma argument and Fin/natural condition elaboration. The exact failed body/prototype/log and identical first drafts are preserved. Agent repairs supply direct numeric arithmetic and typed natural tests; every declaration statement is unchanged. Second5770 exited0 with32 standard-only or axiom-free traces."
